  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/...\n\nLingering showers finally exit on Wednesday as the H5 stacked low \nretrogrades a bit to the west. Expect a cool day with most areas \nhaving highs in the 50s to near 60F. Areas in northeast Nebraska \nremain cooler in the upper 40s. Thursday could still see some \ninfluence from the disturbance with some models suggesting some \nlight showers affecting our far northeast areas, but chances remain \nless than 20%. An H5 shortwave will eject from the NV/UT region \ntoward the Central Plains that day too, but model guidance keeps the \nfeature and any precip activity farther south into Kansas. \n\nSfc high pressure moves in for Friday with dry weather expected and \nhighs in the 50s and 60s. By Saturday and Sunday, models are \nsuggestive of another H5 shortwave ejecting from southwest \nCanada toward the Northern Plains. Significant model spread is \nseen though, so confidence and timing on any precip chances for\nany specific areas remains low at this time.",
